# Select optional authority

Required and optional action selections belong in native IDL, not a TypeScript
`uses` object or Rust builder. For example, a separate caller can request the
Orders RPC without making it mandatory:

```trellis
participant "acme.optional-caller" app {
  use optional orders "acme.orders@v1" {
    call rpc "Orders.Create";
  }
}
```

The referenced API must still be available when compiling the project. Optional
does not mean an unresolved build dependency, an automatic network fallback, or
a guarantee that a running provider exists. It means that the participant can be
authorized without that action selection being granted.

After `trellis generate`, the caller facade has `ordersCreate`, but calling it
without accepted optional authority is denied. Handle the returned `Result` and
show or disable the optional feature according to your application's behavior.
Do not use generated method presence as evidence of a grant.

Use `use required` for the authority the participant needs to fulfill its role.
Changing required or optional selections changes participant needs: regenerate
the artifact and review the deployment authority rather than editing permissions
or digests in application code.
